---
// src/pages/magnificent-tales/index.astro
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import "../styles/pages/magnificent-tales-of-doomed-kingdoms.css";

const HeaderBannerColor = "var(--color-text-light)";
const HeaderTaglineColor = "var(--color-text-light-muted)";
const HeaderNavLinkColor = "var(--color-text-light)";
const backgroundColor = "var(--canvas-magnificent-tales)";

// import goldSeal from "../../assets/gold-seal.png"; // If you have the award badge asset isolated
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Magnificent Tales of Doomed Kingdoms | Rupendra Dhillon"
  description="An ambitious, challenging book that brilliantly evokes a classical mood and time period."
  backgroundColor={backgroundColor}
  HeaderBannerColor={HeaderBannerColor}
  HeaderTaglineColor={HeaderTaglineColor}
  HeaderNavLinkColor={HeaderNavLinkColor}
>
  <div class="tales-landing">
    <header class="tales-header">
      <span class="sub-banner">THE REVIEWS ARE IN !</span>
    </header>

    <section class="reviews-container">
      <div class="review-featured">
        <span class="drop-cap">K</span>
        <blockquote>
          "An ambitious, challenging book that brilliantly evokes a classical
          mood and time period."
          <cite>— Kirkus Reviews</cite>
        </blockquote>
      </div>

      <div class="review-row review-with-seal">
        <div class="review-text-block">
          <p>
            "Author Rupendra Dhillon captures an adventurous spirit that we
            often only associate with classic literature like the tales of Ali
            Baba, King Arthur, and the works of Chaucer."
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="review-seal-block">
          <img
            src="/images/2025-11-20-magnificent-tales-of-doomed-kingdoms/5star-shiny-web.png"
            alt="Readers' Favorite Five Stars Award Seal"
            class="award-seal"
          />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="review-row text-right font-serif-wide">
        <p>
          "Imagine Game of Thrones without the fantastical elements, and you
          will end up with something like the Magnificent Tales of Doomed
          Kingdoms."
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="review-row text-left italic-light">
        <p>
          "I appreciated Dhillon's ability to reveal the humanity, the good, and
          the bad in these characters... There is more to nobility than being
          born into it."
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="review-row text-right italic-light">
        <p>
          “... a real treat for fans of historical prose with an element of
          suspense and family drama.”
        </p>
        <p class="source-subtext">— Readers' Favorite</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="philosophical-teasers">
      <div class="teaser-block center-align">
        <p>Have you ever thought how being a ruler felt like?</p>
      </div>

      <div class="teaser-block right-align teaser-with-image">
        <div class="teaster-block-image-block">
          <img
            src="/images/2025-11-20-magnificent-tales-of-doomed-kingdoms/GettyImages-1372599733-WebOptimized.jpg"
            alt="Readers' Favorite Five Stars Award Seal"
            class="teaster-block-image"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="teaster-block-text">
          <p>
            Have you ever imagined the pain of a ruler who had to discipline
            their children?
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="teaser-block left-align teaser-with-image">
        <div class="teaster-block-text">
          <p>
            How can war, death, hunger, sickness, murder, and grief ruin a
            kingdom at the peak of its glory?
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="teaster-block-image-block">
          <img
            src="/images/2025-11-20-magnificent-tales-of-doomed-kingdoms/GettyImages-1356605472-WebOptimized.jpg"
            alt="Readers' Favorite Five Stars Award Seal"
            class="teaster-block-image"
          />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="teaser-block center-align">
        <div class="teaster-block-text">
          <p>What would you sacrifice for your country and your dynasty?</p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="teaster-block-image-block teaster-block-image-block-center-aligned"
        >
          <img
            src="/images/2025-11-20-magnificent-tales-of-doomed-kingdoms/GettyImages-1374547257-WebOptimized.jpg"
            alt="Readers' Favorite Five Stars Award Seal"
            class="teaster-block-image-center-aligned"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="book-showcase-module">
      <div class="showcase-grid">
        <div class="cover-column">
          <Image
            src="/images/2025-11-20-magnificent-tales-of-doomed-kingdoms/Magnificent+Tales+of+Doomed+Kingdoms_Front+Cover_V2_JPG.jpg"
            alt="Magnificent Tales of Doomed Kingdoms Book Cover"
            class="showcase-cover"
            width={400}
            height={600}
          />
        </div>

        <div class="details-column">
          <h1 class="book-main-title">Magnificent Tales of Doomed Kingdoms</h1>
          <p class="author-attribution">BY RUPENDRA DHILLON</p>

          <div class="book-synopsis">
            <p>
              The book starts from a tale of the unexpected turns a war can take
              and how various relationships can ruin a kingdom at the peak of
              its glory. It is a tale of death, war, hunger, sickness, murder,
              and grief but it also speaks of victory, sacrifice, loyalty, and
              love.
            </p>
            <p>
              Next, we recount the sacrifices that the rulers and their families
              have to make to grow their kingdom from modest beginnings to
              powerful empires. It talks of children who had outgrow their
              childhood in days to assume the role of a ruler and the years
              spent living away from their families so that the kingdom can
              prosper.
            </p>
            <p>
              Finally, we go through the personal struggles of the rulers trying
              to bring up their children so that they can become rightful rulers
              in a world surrounded by their enemies. It tells of victories that
              are worth nothing compared to the unrecoverable losses. It talks
              of acts that would otherwise be considered unimaginable and of the
              turns of fate that can spell disaster for the kingdom.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="amazon-purchase-section">
      <h2 class="purchase-heading"><a href="#">Buy Kindle eBook</a></h2>

      <div class="amazon-buttons-grid">
        <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BKFC7C2M" class="amazon-btn"
          >BUY ON<br />AMAZON.COM</a
        >
        <a href="https://www.amazon.ca/dp/B0BKFC7C2M" class="amazon-btn"
          >BUY ON<br />AMAZON.CA</a
        >
        <a href="http://www.amazon.co.uk/dp/B0BKFC7C2M" class="amazon-btn"
          >BUY ON<br />AMAZON.CO.UK</a
        >
        <a href="https://www.amazon.in/dp/B0BKFC7C2M" class="amazon-btn"
          >BUY ON<br />AMAZON.IN</a
        >
        <a href="http://www.amazon.com.au/dp/B0BKFC7C2M" class="amazon-btn"
          >BUY ON<br />AMAZON.COM.AU</a
        >
      </div>
    </section>
    <!-- TODO: Implement email subscription mechanism later -->
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
